{"title":"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_22\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 22</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_22\">Problem 22</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 22\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A player chooses one of the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. After the choice has been made, two regular four-sided (tetrahedral) dice are rolled, with the sides of the dice numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb15a16cca90d201094265ee529e9e2cfb113de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> If the number chosen appears on the bottom of exactly one die after it has been rolled, then the player wins <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollar. If the number chosen appears on the bottom of both of the dice, then the player wins <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars. If the number chosen does not appear on the bottom of either of the dice, the player loses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollar. What is the expected return to the player, in dollars, for one roll of the dice?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3217106e68d41d5242e630f89a34aa9615a19b88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } -\\frac{1}{8} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } -\\frac{1}{16} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{16} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"430\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be5867f704e37c6578ec1148398c21821a9567e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> ways for your number to show up once, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76fe31c8abe611e194e05cc4edbb9378573eb602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\cdot 1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> way for your number to show up twice, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08f8b84240fbf97ba60819f475b53b1a2295b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 3 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> ways for your number to not show up at all. Think of this as a set of sixteen numbers with six <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s, one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and nine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />'s. The average of this set is the expected return to the player.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75be7467f74e920f61e20d6784fe11fd29f6872a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{6(1)+1(2)-9(1)}{16} = \\frac{6+2-9}{16} = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(B) \\ } -\\frac{1}{16}}\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We approach this through casework. We have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64e32a43ec15d3fe0bde0077b68dffbf025506c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" /> chance of earning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollar. We have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/444c68dd724bfd929ea4674c357a930fa639f343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"37\" height=\"37\" /> chance of earning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars, and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d05c630587c9c3cb17ed17a64252008d9efe8d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"37\" height=\"38\" /> chance of losing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollar. Thus, our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a8be87f732e6861828ca10823c38503a99d3f63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{8} \\cdot 1 + \\frac{1}{16} \\cdot 2 + \\frac{9}{16} \\cdot -1 = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(B) \\ } -\\frac{1}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"295\" height=\"48\" />  -SuperJJ\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B\">2007 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017144938\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 208/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4220/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.085      1 -total\n 58.16%    7.610      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 40.90%    5.351      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with 